{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scriptId": "pl-09-marked-price-discount-profit",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Marked Price, Discount and Profit",
    "description": "Connect cost price, marked price, discount and final selling price in one clear price ladder.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use a four-step price ladder: C.P. → markup → M.P. → discount → S.P. Teach forward and reverse movement, required markup for target profit, no-discount comparisons and why equal markup/discount rates do not cancel.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 12, Profit and Loss. Approved scope: Teach the ladder C.P. → marked price → discount → S.P. Start from one markup and one discount, then reverse to find M.P., C.P., discount or required markup for a target profit. Cover marked price given as a percentage above cost, discount as a percentage of marked price, no-discount profit comparisons, and rupee discount amounts. Show why equal markup and discount percentages do not cancel because they use different bases. Include exam-style questions with list/labelled price terminology."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn marked price, discount and profit.\n\nA tag says ₹1200, the customer gets 20% off, and the shop paid ₹800. The discount is measured from the tag; the profit is measured from the cost. Mixing those bases is the trap.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Marked price is the price written on the tag. Discount is taken from that tag price; profit is judged only after comparing the final S.P. with C.P.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Marked ₹1000, discount 10% → S.P. ₹900.\nIf C.P. ₹750, profit = ₹150 → 20% profit.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
